{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And Timnah was a concubine.</b> After Scripture mentioned the principal seed of Esav, which is the sons of Adah and the sons of Oholivmah, who are the sons of the chief wives, it mentioned that Amalek was among the sons of Esav but not among the sons of the chief wives, only from the concubine whose name was Timnah. Scripture comes to teach us that this Amalek, the son of the maidservant, is not reckoned among the seed of Esav, which is the sons of the chief wives, in the manner written concerning Yishmael (Genesis 21:10): ״כי לא יירש בן האמה הזאת עם בני עם יצחק״. And Scripture needed to inform us that Timnah was a concubine to Eliphaz son of Esav and she is the mother of Amalek, because the sons of Seir the Horite intermarried with the sons of Esav and the families were intermingled. And the Torah and the commandment come after this to warn us to be careful concerning the sons of Esav, that we not take their land and not abhor them, for Esav is Edom, as it is written (Deuteronomy 23:8): ״לא תתעב אדומי״. But concerning Amalek He commanded us to ban and to wipe out their name, in the manner written (Deuteronomy 25:19): ״תמחה את זכר עמלק״. And so that we may know and recognize the families with which we were commanded — which family we are obligated to destroy, and which we are obligated to leave and not harm — Scripture needed to inform us that Amalek, who came to fight against us when Yisrael went out of Egypt, is the son of Timnah the concubine; he is not reckoned among the seed of Esav and is not among the sons of the chief wives, so that we conduct ourselves toward each nation according to the Torah and the commandment. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted that Esav came upon the wife of Seir and she bore this Timnah, and therefore Scripture did not count Timnah among the sons of Seir, for she was the daughter of Seir's wife, not the daughter of Seir; and for this reason it says (verse 22): ״ואחות לוטן תמנע״ — for she was the sister of Lotan, not the daughter of Seir his father. And Scripture teaches you that from this lowly and blemished maidservant Timnah there emerged the wicked Amalek, who began to be a painful thorn in Yisrael's side. And behold, she was a concubine to Eliphaz and she was his sister, his father's daughter; and this Eliphaz begot from her a son, and she died as she gave birth, in her difficult labor in bearing him, and they called the son Timnah after the name of his mother, in order to recall her name. Therefore you will find this name among the sons of Esav, as it is written: ״אלוף תמנע אלוף עלוה״, for this chief was the son of Eliphaz, the son of Timnah his concubine. And the section adjacent to this one, which is ״אלה בני שעיר החורי״, was written only because it says in it ״ואחות לוטן תמנע״, and it comes to teach us that this Timnah was the sister of chiefs, and she wished to attach herself to the seed of Avraham and to be one of them as a concubine, and this is to testify to the greatness of the patriarchs." "<b>And know</b> that from the verse ותמנע a name of eight words goes forth, the number of whose letters is forty. And those who know say that his power to take vengeance on the seed of Esav, and they say: ארבעים יכנו — forty shall strike him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:05.100605085Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}